  "query_preview": "..High pressure amplifies over eastern Arizona for the \nremainder of this weekend and into the early part of next week. A \nweak s/wv over the central Rockies this afternoon may lead to some \nspotty VIRGA development, but that is about it, as the air mass \nstabilizes after today.\n\nA trough enters the Great Basin by the middle of next week. This \nwill enhance our winds a little bit and drop daytime temperatures. \nHowever, this will still be a mainly dry pattern and temperatures \nwill still be above normal.\n\nA more zonal, but warm and continued dry pattern then develops for \nthe end of next week and even the following weekend.",
